Harbor: three small corrections to earlier patches, and three limits of them written down (#83).

Fixed here:

- 0002 (byte-sized syscall arguments): NtCreateEvent's BOOLEAN "state" was the one narrow by-value argument
  without SYSCALL_NARROW_ARG; it was missed because the function's name is wrapped in GPT_IMPORT(). The current
  build happened to be right (clang emits movzbl before the store), another compiler needn't be.
  Test: WindowsTests/abi/run.sh ("NtCreateEvent with dirty upper bits").

- 0003 (UDP connect to port 0): the retry on port 9 also ran for the unspecified address. Windows takes a
  datagram connect to 0.0.0.0:0 or [::]:0 as "disconnect"; macOS connects 0.0.0.0:9 to this Mac's own port 9,
  after which the socket drops datagrams from every other sender. The unspecified address is no longer retried:
  the call fails with WSAEADDRNOTAVAIL as in Wine on macOS without 0003, and the socket stays as it was. (It
  is not turned into a real disconnect: a socket that was connected before stays connected.)
  Test: WindowsTests/net/run.sh ("UDP still receives after connect to 0.0.0.0:0").

- 0006/0008 (program names): 0008 kept ".", ".." and "ntdll.so" out of usable_app_name(), but the fallback
  that names the loader link after the program's file, extract_exe_name(), took them: "ntdll.so.exe" was started
  through the link directory's own ntdll.so link, and "..exe" through the directory itself, i.e. not at all.
  Names that start with a dot and "ntdll.so" (any case) now get no link; the program runs as "wine".
  Test: WindowsTests/appname/run.sh.

Known limits, not changed:

- 0001 (drawing into another process's window): a process has 8 surfaces for such windows, replaced in turn.
  If it holds DCs for more than 8 windows of other processes at once, the DC whose surface was replaced is not
  flushed by its ReleaseDC (release_dc looks the surface up by window and no longer finds it); what was drawn
  through it never reaches the screen. Using more than 8 such windows one after the other is fine. No program is
  known to do this; a fix needs the surface to be found from the DC rather than from a fixed table.

- 0006 (program names): pe_file_app_name() reads the executable's version resource through mmap in the process
  that calls CreateProcess. A file that is truncated by someone else between the fstat and the read raises
  SIGBUS in that process. All offsets are checked against the size at open, so only truncation during these few
  reads is affected. Reading with pread instead would mean reading the headers, the section table and the
  resource tree piecewise; not done.

- 0014 (user name "harbor"): advapi32 decides between "crossover" and "harbor" by looking at
  C:\users\crossover, while shell32 builds the same path from the registry's ProfilesDirectory. The two agree
  as long as the profiles folder is C:\users, which is what every Harbor bottle has; in a bottle whose
  ProfilesDirectory was changed, GetUserName and %USERPROFILE% can name different users.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -552,6 +552,12 @@
         exe_name_len = p - exe_name;
     else
         exe_name_len = strlen(exe_name);
+
+    /* HARBOR HACK: the name becomes a link beside the "ntdll.so" link in the loader link directory. Never
+     * ".", ".." or that one ("ntdll.so.exe" would be started through the ntdll.so link, i.e. not at all): the
+     * same names usable_app_name() in process.c refuses. Such a program runs under the loader's own name. */
+    if (exe_name[0] == '.' || (exe_name_len == 8 && !strncasecmp(exe_name, "ntdll.so", 8)))
+        exe_name_len = 0;
 
     if (exe_name_len)
         ret = strndup(exe_name, exe_name_len);  /* HARBOR HACK: without the extension, as the comment above says */
